A||||3||JohnnyK||I need a sod (thief) expert! :)||||14||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||03-21-2001||12:21 AM||||I had a long "accident" this winter that ended up leaving a few litres (well, maybe 6-8) of oil in the grass next to my driveway. I filled up my oil pan (the ones you use for changing oil) and left it outside. Well, snow got into it, it expanded, and by springtime, there was only water left in it, and the oil was everywhere else. I have to use acid on my driveway, but this was my plan for the grass. Dig about 2 feet down in all the culprit areas, and then replace with sod! ANyone know how to snag some sod? I need to do it from my nearby field. Do I cut a square, and slip a long knife under it or something?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000001||btoth||03-21-2001||11:39 AM||||Not too sure, but one night my friends stole a bunch of sod from somewhere and laid it out on somebody's driveway. The funny thing is that I guess the person found the sod (obviously!) the next day and used it on their lawn!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000002||Hank is Here||03-21-2001||04:59 PM||||Simple just go to a rental store and rent a sod cutter.  They are gas powered and do a good job.  Just cut out your bad stuff and cut another swath of the same type of grass somewhere.  If you can do it as early as possible before the grass starts growing.  Just make sure to cut the same type of grass.  The blade from the machine comes down on two sides and then has the main center cross piece about 18" wide which cuts the roots from under the grass.  The grass rolls up in nice balls. Sorry I don't know how to cut the roots from underneeth by hand.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroBUZZ||03-21-2001||08:01 PM||||How big an area do you need to do?  Make sure you get all the oily soil out and replace it with some quality topsoil. If you cut your own sod you can use a square (flat front) spade. Cut out the sod you want say a foot and a half by 4 or 5 feet. Start at one end and use the end of the spade to slice under the roots and roll it up as you go( probably 3 or 4 in thick).  If it's just a small spot go whole hog and buy a couple of rolls of the real thing.<BR>Gary||||reg||5
